📊 IoT Temperature & Humidity Monitoring System — Progress Report
✅ 1. Hardware Setup
Device: ESP8266 microcontroller + DHT11 sensor

Function: Reads temperature & humidity every 60 seconds

Code: Arduino sketch that:

Connects to Wi-Fi

Reads sensor values

Sends data as JSON via HTTP POST

✅ 2. Cloud Backend on EC2 (Flask + SQLite)
Flask API running on EC2 instance

Endpoints:

POST /api/data: Receives JSON data from ESP8266

GET /api/latest: Returns the latest sensor reading

GET /api/history: Returns last N readings for charting

Data stored in: SQLite database (sensor.db)

Table: readings(id, temperature, humidity, timestamp)

✅ 3. Web Dashboard (HTML + JavaScript)
Hosted on the same EC2 server via Flask

Displays:

Live Temperature, Humidity, and Timestamp (updates every 5s)

A line graph using Chart.js showing last 50 readings

✅ Tech Stack Overview
Layer	Technology
Microcontroller	ESP8266 + DHT11
Transport	HTTP POST (JSON)
Backend	Python + Flask + SQLite
Frontend	HTML + JS + Chart.js
Hosting	AWS EC2 (Linux)

🧠 Skills Practiced So Far
IoT sensor programming (ESP8266, DHT11)

